1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,800
In the lobby, an old radio on the
front desk is still talking.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:10,000
This is an emergency broadcast. Stay
where you are. Help is on the way.
This message will repeat.

3
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:13,167
Help is on the way. Sure. Help for
who?

4
00:00:13,867 --> 00:00:17,500
Eleven AM. Zero bars on the phone.
Every TV channel is static.

5
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:22,033
Okay. Think. What do I actually need?
Not news. Not answers.

6
00:00:22,733 --> 00:00:26,200
Rule two. Fill the bathtub first.
Water before news.

7
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:32,667
Without power, the city pumps slow
down, then stop. The tap coughs,
spits, and gives you a trickle.

8
00:00:33,367 --> 00:00:40,600
A full tub is about forty gallons. A
month of drinking water, if I'm
careful. Pots next. Then every bottle
I own.
